                            when="1944-11-15">November 15, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Proposal for Section C of the Chapter on the
                        Security Council</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#flush">C. <hi rendition="#italic">Voting</hi>
                </p>
                <p>1. Each member of the Security Council should have one vote.</p>
                <p>2. Decisions of the Security Council on procedural matters should be made by an
                    affirmative vote of seven members.</p>
                <p>3. Decisions of the Security Council on all other matters should be made by an
                    affirmative vote of seven members including the concurring votes of the
                    permanent members; provided that, in decisions under Section VIII A and under
                    paragraph 1 of Section VIII C, a party to a dispute should abstain from
                    voting.</p>
            </div>
